        "rationale": "Keeps a single unsharded `e2e` job, installs only Chromium with its deps (headless shell, valid for the headless-only config) and drops the one-worker pin, with the case built on step timings across all four main runs and both shard runs; minor deductions for hard-coding `--workers=4` on a 4-vCPU runner rather than a measured or default setting, for apparently attributing the late third shard to the 83s run rather than the 117s one, and for the change being unverified on a runner."
