        "rationale": "Clearly tabulates the ~15s/~50s fixed cost against the 32-37s of tests with the runs they came from, explains that each shard re-paid the install and that a late third shard held one run up, names the unused-browser install and the single worker as the removed costs, and gives an honestly hedged 40-55s estimate; but it omits the split-by-count point, the tripled runner minutes and the noise between the two shard samples, and understates that one sharded run was slower than not sharding at all."
